      <div type="clause" n="18">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 18</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>XVI.<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="27" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.27"/> Gif hwa nunnan mid hæmeðþinge<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="28" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.28"/> oððe on hire hrægl oððe on hire breost butan hire leafe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="29" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.29"/> gefó, sie<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="30" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.30"/> hit twybete swa we ær be læwdum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="31" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.31"/> men fundon.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-h"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>XVI. Gif hwa nunnan mid hæmedðinge oððe on hire hrægl oððe on hire breost buton<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.1"/> hire leafe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="9" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.9"/> gefó, sy<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.2"/> hit twybote<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="10" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.10"/> swa we ær anfandlice<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="11" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.11"/> be læwedum monnum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.1"/> fundon.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-b-no-prol"><pb n="58" ed="#liebermann"/>Be nunnena andfencgu<hi rend="italic">m</hi>. Gyf hwa nunnan mid hæmedðinge oððe<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="6" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.6"/> hire hrægl oððe on hire breost buton hire leafe g<hi rend="italic">e</hi>fó, sy hit twibote swa we ǽr be læwedu<hi rend="italic">m</hi> men fundon.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="18" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="59" ed="#liebermann"/>Si<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="19" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.19"/> quis<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="20" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.20"/> nunnam causa fornicationis in uestes aut in sinum sine<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="21" target="#Af_18.lnote.oe.21"/> licentia comprehendat, sit hoc duplo emendabile sicut ante simpliciter de laica decreuimus.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="72" ed="#attenborough"/>[Be nunnena andfencgum.] Gif hwa nunnan mid hæmeðþinge<ptr type="editorNote" n="8" target="#Af_18.attnote.fn.8"/> oððe on hire hrægl oððe on hire breost butan hire leafe gefó, sie hit twybete<ptr type="editorNote" n="9" target="#Af_18.attnote.fn.9"/> swa we ær be<ptr type="editorNote" n="10" target="#Af_18.attnote.fn.10"/> læwdum men<ptr type="editorNote" n="11" target="#Af_18.attnote.fn.11"/> fundon.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="20" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="310" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>{XVI} Gif hwa nunnan mid hæmeðþinge oððe on hire hrægl oððe on hire breost butan hire leaf gefó, sie hit twybete swa we ær be læwdum men fundon.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="59" ed="#liebermann"/>Wenn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Af_18.lnote.de.1"/> einer einer Nonne<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Af_18.lnote.de.2"/> buhlerischer Weise entweder an ihr Kleid oder an ihre Brust ohne ihre Erlaubniss fasst, sei das doppelt so busspflichtig<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Af_18.lnote.de.3"/>, wie wir<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Af_18.lnote.de.4"/> vorhin<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="5" target="#Af_18.lnote.de.5"/> über eine Laienperson bestimmten.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">If someone seizes a nun lustfully either by her clothing or by her breast without her permission, let that be twice as liable to compensation as we determined before concerning a lay person.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#attenborough" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="73" ed="#attenborough"/>If anyone lustfully seizes a nun, either by her clothes or by her breast, without her permission, he shall pay as compensation twice the sum we have fixed in the case of a woman belonging to the laity.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock"><pb n="412" ed="#whitelock"/>If anyone in lewd fashion seizes a nun either by her clothes or her breast without her leave, the compensation is to be double that we have established for a lay person.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" corresp="#wit-e"><pb n="311" ed="#jurasinski-and-oliver"/>If someone seizes a nun with carnal intent either on her clothing or on her breast without her permission, let the compensation be twice what we earlier set for lay[wo]men.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="270"><label>cites</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11">Af 11–11.2</ref> <quote>Note too that Af 18 (lewd approaches to nuns) and 26 (under-age rape) actually cite 11, 11:2 (equivalent for laity/adult)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#wormald-mel" n="272"><label>cross-reference</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11">Af 11–11.2</ref> <quote>18 (ref. 11 – 11:2)</quote></note>
        <note type="comparison" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="311"><label>cf.</label> <ref target="clause:Af_11">Af 11</ref> <quote>§13 sets the fine for touching a laywoman's breast at 5 shillings.</quote></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#jurasinski-and-oliver" n="307"><ref target="clause:Af_11">Af 11</ref></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.27" n="27" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Capitel</hi> 18 <hi rend="italic">setzt vor</hi> 12 <hi rend="italic">So; vgl. Quadr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">So places chapter 18 before 12; cf. Quadr.</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.28" n="28" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">hæmedþ. <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">hæmedþ. So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.29" n="29" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">læfe <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">læfe Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.30" n="30" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">sy hit twybót <hi rend="italic">Ld</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">sy hit twybót Ld</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.31" n="31" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">læwed. <hi rend="italic">Ld;</hi> lewed. <hi rend="italic">So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">læwed. Ld; lewed. So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">geändert in</hi> a</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o altered to a</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.9" n="9" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">geänd. aus</hi> leofe</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">altered from leofe</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">y <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">y on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.10" n="10" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">o <hi rend="italic">auf Rasur</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">o on an erasure</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.11" n="11" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">erster Buchst. undeutlich, vielleicht einer Glosse nachgemalt, die</hi> anfealdlice <hi rend="italic">lautete oder doch meinte und auch Quadr. vorlag</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">first letter indistinct, perhaps copied from a gloss which read, or at any rate meant, anfealdlice, and which Quadr. also had before him</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.19" n="19" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Cap.</hi> 18 <hi rend="italic">steht vor</hi> 12 <hi rend="italic">Lond; vgl. So</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Lond places cap. 18 before 12; cf. So</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.20" n="20" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">fehlt R T</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">lacking in R T</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.21" n="21" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">59</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">s.l. <hi rend="italic">fehlt K</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">s.l. lacking in K</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.oe.6" n="6" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">58</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">ergänze</hi> on</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">supply on</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Dies Kapitel folgt in So Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> auf 11, 5; <hi rend="italic">s. o.</hi> 12¹. ‘Über Angriffe auf Nonnen’ Rb B; <hi rend="italic">vgl. Wb: -d</hi> unorganisch hinter <hi rend="italic">n</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">In So Q <hi rend="smallcaps">i</hi> this chapter follows 11, 5; <hi rend="italic">see above</hi> 12¹. ‘Of assaults on nuns’ Rb B; <hi rend="italic">cf. Wb: -d</hi> inorganic after <hi rend="italic">n</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.de.2" n="2" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Nonne 12—14. Hinzuzudenken ist ein Strafgeld an den König als den Schutzherrn und, sofern sie öffentlich klagte, an den Richter</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Cf. Gl</hi> Nonne 12—14. To be added in thought is a fine to the king as protector and, if she brought a public complaint, to the judge</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.de.3" n="3" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Adj. in E, Subst. in HB</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Adj. in E, noun in HB</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.de.4" n="4" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Af 11</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Af 11</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Af_18.lnote.de.5" n="5" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">55</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">‘einfach’ fügt zu HQ, um Af’s Doppelsinn zu vermeiden; denn <hi rend="italic">swa</hi> könnte ‘ebenso’ heissen</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">HQ add ‘simply’, to avoid Af’s ambiguity; for <hi rend="italic">swa</hi> could mean ‘likewise’</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_18.attnote.fn.8" n="8" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>hæmeðþinge</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">hæmedþinge</hi>. B, H &amp; So.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_18.attnote.fn.9" n="9" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>twybete</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">twybote</hi>. H. <hi rend="italic">twibote</hi>. B.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_18.attnote.fn.10" n="10" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>be</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">anfandlice be l</hi>. H.</seg></note>
        <note type="editorNote" subtype="footnote" xml:id="Af_18.attnote.fn.11" n="11" source="#attenborough"><bibl><biblScope unit="page">72</biblScope></bibl><label>men</label><seg type="original" xml:lang="en"><hi rend="italic">monnum</hi>. H.</seg></note>
      </div>
